-- ============================================================================
-- 36: HUD hudq=0 ROOT CAUSE + the SHIP-THE-ENGINE-HUD recommendation (research).
-- The render-replica live HUD is procedural because the HUDQ tail is EMPTY on prod.
-- This pins WHY (deploy/env gap, NOT a capture bug) and recommends shipping the
-- engine's own HUD TA quads over reconstructing them. feat/render-replica-live.
-- Pinned 2026-06-14. RESEARCH finding (no code rewrite).
-- ============================================================================
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:hudq_prod_binary_audit SET kind='oracle',
  ref='ssh root@149.28.44.118: md5sum /usr/local/bin/flycast + /opt/maplecast/flycast-hudq-staged; systemctl show maplecast-headless.service -p Environment; strings | grep MAPLECAST_HUD_TA',
  note='LIVE PROD AUDIT 2026-06-14. Running binary md5=8a4566083e9aa93a2e9d8fc7fc4423c1; staged HUDQ binary md5=48364cd8d128de2b620ed749c2cb0a8d (== the dev build in finding:replica_live_hud_real_ta_validated). They DIFFER: the running binary is NOT the HUDQ build. `strings /usr/local/bin/flycast | grep MAPLECAST_HUD_TA` returns NOTHING (no HUD-QDIAG/mc_hud_qdiag.log/MAPLECAST_HUD_TA_* symbols) -> the live binary PREDATES the HUDQ feature entirely. The staged binary HAS all the symbols. systemd Environment= has MAPLECAST_ASMTRACE=1, MAPLECAST_ORACLE_PROBE=1, MAPLECAST_FRAME_ORACLE_HOOK=1 but NO MAPLECAST_HUD_TA. So even if the staged binary were swapped in, the env gate (mc_hudTaEnabled = getenv("MAPLECAST_HUD_TA")!=nullptr, maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp:951) is unset -> collectHud is a no-op (mc_oracle_collectHud early-returns s_nhud=0) -> the HUDQ tail is absent -> client hudQuads=[] -> procedural fallback. TWO independent reasons the tail is empty, BOTH deploy/config, NEITHER a capture-logic bug.';

UPSERT finding:hudq_empty_root_cause SET
  statement='hudq=0 (window.__hudQuadCount()===0) ROOT CAUSE = DEPLOYMENT + ENV GAP, not a capture bug. The HUDQ capture (collectHudQuads, finding:replica_live_hud_real_ta) is fully built, validated quad-level (78 kept HUD quads vs the QDIAG inventory), and STAGED to prod, but: (1) the LIVE prod binary /usr/local/bin/flycast (md5 8a456608) PREDATES HUDQ entirely — `strings` shows zero MAPLECAST_HUD_TA symbols; the HUDQ-capable build (md5 48364cd8) sits unused at /opt/maplecast/flycast-hudq-staged and the service was never restarted onto it (per finding:replica_live_hud_real_ta_validated: "live service was NOT restarted, user-coordinated"). (2) the systemd Environment lacks MAPLECAST_HUD_TA, so mc_hudTaEnabled is false and collectHud no-ops even on the right binary. The CLIENT side is already complete: replay.html parses the HUDQ magic (0x48554451), fills hudQuads[], renderHudQuads() draws them via the SAME pvr2 path as bodies (buildHudTA), and renderHudPass() prefers it over the procedural reconstruction when hudQuads.length>0 (web/render-replica/replay.html:533-632,1275-1296). So the wire interface and the draw path are both wired and waiting; nothing more is needed client-side for the bars/timer/meter/portrait quads. CONCRETE FIX (server-only, no code change): swap the staged binary in (md5-verify == 48364cd8) AND add MAPLECAST_HUD_TA=1 to /etc/maplecast/headless.env, restart maplecast-headless.service, confirm /dev/shm has a non-empty capture and window.__hudQuadCount()>0 (expect ~78). Optionally arm MAPLECAST_QDIAG=1 for one run to dump /dev/shm/mc_hud_qdiag.log and re-run tools/validate_hud_ta.py --hudq for the byte-for-byte PASS.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

UPSERT source:hud_render_routine_rom SET kind='code',
  ref='marvelous2 bank0f loc_8C0F06E0 (#data bank15.loc_8c15FFB0) + loc_8C0F06EC (in-match HUD dispatch) + bank15 loc_8c15FFB0 (bar team-modulate) + bank16 loc_8c1604Ce/loc_8c1601B4 (HUD draw) + loc_8C0F0FDC (METER_MAX=144); bank16 loc_8c160a70 (HUD message table) / loc_8c160a30 (VITAL/results text #data) confirmed present locally',
  note='THE ENGINE REAL HUD RENDER (ground truth our procedural HUD fakes). The in-match HUD is built by the bank0f dispatch (loc_8C0F06E0 references bank15.loc_8c15FFB0 + the cell processor bank12 loc_8c1294C8 + bank16 draw routines) and emitted as PVR TA polys into the SURVIVING (HUD/composite) STARTRENDER pass — the one flycast QueueRender keeps (op~573 tr~42, isRTT=0) while it DROPS the character/body pass (op~265 tr~2024). CONFIRMED poly inventory from a live in-match prod TA stream (source:hud_ta_qdiag_inventory): ALL HUD polys are PVR para type 4 (Polygon, NOT type-5 Sprite), textured, fmt=1 (FONT glyph atlas, TCW 0x0809BE00) or fmt=2 (portrait/icon, TCW 0x0809DE00/E000), Offset=1, Col_Type INTENSITY float base=1.0 — so per-team bar TINT comes from the FONT/glyph TEXTURE + the loc_8c15FFB0 vertex modulate, NOT an ARGB8888 per-team modulate. The life bar / super meter are NOT distinct sprites: a WHITE-texel polygon modulated by a per-team-slot vertex colour (loc_8c15FFB0: magenta/green/cyan per active point char C1/C2/C3). The HUD textures (FONT.BIN font + boxed digits + portrait glyphs) are decoded into VRAM at MATCH LOAD, before any in-match STARTRENDER, so every HUDQ tcw resolves against the already-shipped static 8MB VRAM prefix — the HUDQ tail needs to ship ONLY per-frame screen geometry (corners/UV/colour/control words), zero extra texture wire.';

UPSERT finding:hud_super_meter_real_render SET
  statement='THE SUPER METER "missing layers" — why a single bar looks wrong. The MVC2 hyper combo gauge is a SEGMENTED multi-level (up to 5) gauge: a per-side numeric LEVEL indicator + a fill bar that resets/re-tints each level, with notch/block separators, drawn from the outer corner inward (P1 lower-left / P2 lower-right). The live state is TWO fields, both already in the wire (source:hud_field_addresses): meter_fill (u16 0x8C289646 P1 / 0x8C289648 P2, the CURRENT-level partial fill, 0..METER_MAX=144 per loc_8C0F0FDC) AND meter_level (u8 0x8C28964A P1 / 0x8C28964B P2, the stocked whole levels 0..5). The procedural HUD draws a SINGLE fill/144 bar + level pips, which is geometrically right-ish but lacks the engine`s real segmented art (level blocks, the per-level retint, the EXP/LV gauge labels from FONT.BIN rec1) and the exact angled bar polygon — so it reads as a flat approximation. The engine render = the loc_8c15FFB0 white-tex*vertex-colour bar emitted as the fmt=1/fmt=2 HUD polys captured by HUDQ; shipping those real quads renders the gauge segments/level-retint/labels pixel-exact with no reconstruction. The single-bar reconstruction looks wrong because it collapses a multi-level segmented gauge (level + within-level fill + labels) into one /144 bar.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

UPSERT finding:hud_portraits_real_vs_procedural SET
  statement='THE PORTRAITS "not rotated right" — what the rip contains + the authoritative path. The portrait rip (web/render-replica/hud/portraits/portraits.png, finding:hud_portrait_decode / re_kb 30+35) is decoded OFFLINE from DM01POL/DM01TEX texture #11 (512x512 RGB565 TWIDDLED, 8x8 of 64x64 cells); faces are STORED 90deg-rotated on the sheet and must be de-rotated CCW to upright, and the char_id->cell map is the column-major DC table loc_8c161fec[col*8+row] (NOT PLxx_FAC.BIN, which is an undecoded NaomiLib display list — that HANDOFF note is superseded). So the portrait SOURCE + decode + char_id->cell map are now AUTHORITATIVE and pixel-validated for 47 chars (9 fall to a monogram, never a wrong face). ANY residual "not rotated right" in the live HUD is therefore NOT a decode/source problem — it is the PROCEDURAL hud-client.mjs _plate() drawing the rip with the wrong orientation/crop/anchor, OR a stale cache. The engine`s OWN portrait HUD render is the fmt=2 (TCW 0x0809DE00/E000) portrait/icon polys in the surviving HUD pass — shipping those via HUDQ draws the portrait exactly as the engine orients/crops it (correct rotation baked into the TA UVs), eliminating the procedural orientation guess entirely. Recommendation: rely on HUDQ for the in-match portrait rather than the procedural _plate() rip.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

UPSERT finding:hud_ship_engine_recommendation SET
  statement='RECOMMENDATION (the deliverable): SHIP THE ENGINE`S REAL HUD via the HUDQ tail; STOP reconstructing it. The bodies are byte-exact because they ship the engine`s own per-part geometry (ASMTRACE/CHARQ ground truth); the HUD is wrong because it is a hand-drawn approximation of a textured, segmented, team-modulated TA pass it cannot fully fake (segmented meter + level retint + FONT labels + correctly-oriented portraits + angled parallelogram bars). The HUDQ path is the bodies-style approach applied to the HUD: capture the engine`s OWN surviving-pass HUD quads (collectHudQuads) and draw them via the SAME pvr2 path (renderHudQuads) against the already-shipped static VRAM. It is BUILT, validated quad-level (78 quads), client-complete, and only blocked by a deploy/env gap (finding:hudq_empty_root_cause). HIGHEST-LEVERAGE NEXT STEP (no code change): (1) deploy /opt/maplecast/flycast-hudq-staged -> /usr/local/bin/flycast (md5-verify 48364cd8 before+after, BACKUP first per deploy-headless.sh discipline); (2) add MAPLECAST_HUD_TA=1 (and one-shot MAPLECAST_QDIAG=1) to /etc/maplecast/headless.env; (3) restart maplecast-headless.service; (4) verify window.__hudQuadCount()>0 (~78) live and the procedural fallback stops firing. THEN the only OPEN refinement is tier-2 multi-glyph tri-strip name plates (finding:replica_live_hud_real_ta_open_multistrip) — defer; bars/meter/timer/portraits are single quads and ship correct immediately. The procedural hud-client.mjs stays ONLY as the older-server/HUD-off fallback. STAGE (brief): the stage residual is now a FIDELITY-vs-coverage gap, NOT a projection bug — finding:stage_pernode_matrices_closed proves M1.M2 is correct to 0.000px and the engine-TA bake (finding:stage_control_words_grounded/stage_deck_texture_closed) ships the engine`s REAL per-poly control words + textures for STG0B; the residual is that ONLY STG0B has an engine-TA capture, so other stage_ids fall to the POL-rip deck-only world-space path until each is captured live + baked. Same pattern as HUDQ: shipping the engine`s own TA (per stage) is the higher-fidelity source; the work left is per-stage capture+bake, not a math fix.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

-- ============================================================================
-- 2026-06-14 (LIVE HUDQ now shipping; binary 48364cd8 + MAPLECAST_HUD_TA=1 on prod):
-- two render gaps diagnosed off a LIVE replica-live HUDQ capture (143 quads/frame,
-- tools/render-replica-poc/hudq_capture.mjs) + rendered offline through the SAME pvr2
-- path (tools/render-replica-poc/render_hudq.mjs, Dawn). GAP1 = FONT GARBLE: FIXED.
-- GAP2 = SUPER-METER SEGMENTS: a server-side VRAM-PREFIX COVERAGE gap (flag). Bar TINT
-- confirmed CORRECT (no fix).
-- ============================================================================

UPSERT source:hudq_live_capture_2026_06_14 SET kind='oracle',
  ref='node tools/render-replica-poc/hudq_capture.mjs --url wss://nobd.net/replica-live (saved _hud_cap/{vram_prefix.bin,pvr_frame.bin,hudq_tail.bin,hudq_inventory.txt}); rendered with tools/render-replica-poc/render_hudq.mjs (Dawn/webgpu npm offscreen, pvr2-renderer+texture-manager+ta-parser VERBATIM)',
  note='LIVE HUDQ tail is populated on prod: ~143 quads/frame (was 0 pre-deploy). Quad classes by tcw: FONT name/digit = tcw 0809BE00 (texAddr 0x4DF000, fmt=1 RGB565, scan=0 TWIDDLED, 128x128, uv float) + the LEVEL/TIME digit sheets tcw 0809E1/E2/E3/E7/E8/E9 (texAddr 0x4F0xxx, 32x32 565 twiddled, a 2x2 glyph grid sub-sampled by UV row). PORTRAIT/icon = tcw 0809DE/DF/E0 (texAddr 0x4EFxxx). LIFE/METER bars = tcw 08080000 (texAddr 0x400000 = an 8x8 SOLID-WHITE 565 texel, ALL UVs 0 -> pure vertex-colour fill). SEGMENTED-METER art = fmt=5 PAL4 tcw 2A489xxx (texAddr 0x44Bxxx-0x44Dxxx, palSel 18). VRAM-prefix audit: font/bars/portraits/digit-sheets ALL present + correctly twiddled-565 (font_twiddled.ppm shows readable glyphs); BUT the entire VRAM block 0x440000-0x460000 (the PAL4 meter art) is 100% ZERO in the shipped prefix.';

UPSERT finding:hud_font_garble_strip_order SET
  statement='FONT GARBLE ROOT CAUSE = WRONG TRIANGLE-STRIP CORNER ORDER in buildHudTA (web/render-replica/replay.html), NOT a texture decode/twiddle/palette bug. The FONT.BIN glyph atlas (tcw 0809BE00, texAddr 0x4DF000) is fmt=1 RGB565, scan=0 (twiddled), and pvr2 TextureManager decodes it CORRECTLY — an offline detwiddle dump (twiddled vs linear) yields readable glyphs, proving the twiddle/format/UV path is right. The garble came from buildHudTA emitting the 4 captured corners in strip order [0,1,3,2] (a perimeter-walk assumption). collectHudQuads (maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp) captures the corners in the engine`s OWN SUBMIT order (rc.idx/rc.verts walk) = the engine`s native PVR strip order, so the correct re-tiling is the IDENTITY strip [0,1,2,3] -> the engine`s own two triangles (0,1,2)+(1,2,3). The [0,1,3,2] default put the shared diagonal on the wrong pair, diagonally mis-tiling every (italic, parallelogram) glyph slice -> multi-colour noise. FIX: change the buildHudTA default order from [0,1,3,2] to [0,1,2,3] (window._hudQuadOrder still overrides live). CONFIRMED on the live 143-quad capture rendered through pvr2: [0,1,2,3] -> readable names/timer/LEVEL + correctly-italic font; [0,1,3,2] -> garbled. The dark trailing blocks beside short labels are the empty/dim glyph-cell padding in the 2x2 digit sheet (faithful texture content, not an artifact). Deployed in replay.html buildHudTA.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

UPSERT finding:hud_meter_segments_vram_gap SET
  statement='SUPER-METER "missing segmented level gauge" = a SERVER-SIDE VRAM-PREFIX COVERAGE GAP, not a client render bug and not a capture-list gap. The segmented multi-level gauge art is fmt=5 PAL4 (tcw 2A489xxx, palSel 18) at VRAM texAddr 0x44B000-0x44D800. Those quads ARE present in the live HUDQ tail (inventory quads ~41-58: fmt=5, correct screen corners + UVs + tcw). BUT the shipped static 8MB VRAM prefix has the ENTIRE block 0x440000-0x460000 ZEROED (64KB-block histogram: 0x400000/0x410000 + 0x470000.. carry data; 0x440000-0x460000 carry NONE). So the PAL4 meter texels decode to transparent/black and the segments never appear, while the LEVEL/TIME numeric LABELS (which live in the PRESENT font sheets 0x4F0xxx) DO render. The single flat pink/white bar is the tcw 08080000 white-texel bar tinted by vertex colour (rendering correctly); the segmented fill OVER it is the absent PAL4 layer. FIX IS SERVER-SIDE (flagged for mvc2-sh4-re-expert): extend the shipped VRAM region(s) in the replica-live prefix builder to cover 0x440000-0x460000 (the PAL4 HUD-meter texture bank), OR re-snapshot VRAM after the meter art is decoded at match-load — likely it decodes to a VRAM bank outside the currently-snapshotted ranges, or is written after the prefix snapshot. CLIENT NEEDS NO CHANGE: once those texels ride the prefix, the existing fmt=5 PAL4 decode (texture-manager _pal4, palSel from tcw, palette from pvr tail) + the captured quads render the segmented gauge with zero extra work.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

UPSERT finding:hud_bar_tint_confirmed SET
  statement='PER-TEAM BAR TINT is CORRECT in buildHudTA/pvr2 — no fix needed. The life/meter bars (tcw 08080000) sample an 8x8 SOLID-WHITE 565 texel (decoded white, confirmed) at UV(0,0), so the per-corner vertex colour col[i] drives the fill via white*colour modulation. The captured cols carry the real loc_8c15FFB0 team colours: magenta fefe3ffe (R254 G63 B254) for a point-char health bar gouraud-blending to yellow fefefe00, cyan fe00bffe (R0 G191 B254) for the super, pure red fffe0000 for the chip/drain. Rendering quad-2 (a magenta health bar) ALONE through pvr2 shows the magenta->yellow gouraud EXACTLY, proving the tint applies. The full HUD reads flat-red only because, for this captured HP state, the red chip/drain bar is emitted AFTER and fully OVERLAPS the magenta bar at the same X extent — which is the engine`s OWN submit order + geometry (we draw the engine`s quads in the engine`s order), so it matches the engine for that frame; as HP drains the bars take different widths and the magenta/cyan show. buildHudTA correctly FORCES colType=0 (packed per-vertex BGRA) so col[i] reaches the corners.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

RELATE finding:hud_font_garble_strip_order->cites->source:hudq_live_capture_2026_06_14;
RELATE finding:hud_font_garble_strip_order->cites->source:hud_render_routine_rom;
RELATE finding:hud_meter_segments_vram_gap->cites->source:hudq_live_capture_2026_06_14;
RELATE finding:hud_meter_segments_vram_gap->about->finding:hud_super_meter_real_render;
RELATE finding:hud_bar_tint_confirmed->cites->source:hudq_live_capture_2026_06_14;
RELATE finding:hud_bar_tint_confirmed->cites->source:hud_render_routine_rom;

RELATE finding:hudq_empty_root_cause->cites->source:hudq_prod_binary_audit;
RELATE finding:hudq_empty_root_cause->about->finding:replica_live_hud_real_ta;
RELATE finding:hud_super_meter_real_render->cites->source:hud_field_addresses;
RELATE finding:hud_super_meter_real_render->cites->source:hud_render_routine_rom;
RELATE finding:hud_portraits_real_vs_procedural->about->finding:hud_portrait_decode;
RELATE finding:hud_ship_engine_recommendation->cites->source:hudq_prod_binary_audit;
RELATE finding:hud_ship_engine_recommendation->cites->source:hud_render_routine_rom;
RELATE finding:hud_ship_engine_recommendation->about->finding:replica_live_hud_real_ta;
RELATE finding:hud_ship_engine_recommendation->about->finding:hudq_empty_root_cause;

-- ============================================================================
-- 36b (2026-06-14): GARBLE ROOT CAUSE GROUNDED. The HUDQ tail is now LIVE
-- (running binary md5 48364cd8 == staged HUDQ build, MAPLECAST_HUD_TA=1 IS in
-- the running process env per /proc/PID/environ — SUPERSEDES finding:hudq_empty_root_cause,
-- which was true only at the older md5 8a456608). So the garble is a CLIENT-SIDE
-- DECODE bug on the REAL engine HUD quads that ARE shipping, not an empty tail.
-- ============================================================================

UPSERT source:hud_font_vram_dump SET kind='oracle',
  ref='LIVE PROD VRAM 2026-06-14: ssh root@149.28.44.118 dd if=/dev/shm/mc_vram_dump.bin skip=0x4DF000 (FONT) / 0x4EF000 (portrait/names). Decoded local _decode_hud.py: RGB565 + Morton/PVR detwiddle. Running binary md5 48364cd8, MAPLECAST_HUD_TA=1 confirmed in /proc/PID/environ.',
  note='THE FONT HUD GLYPH TEXTURE, GROUND-TRUTHED FROM LIVE VRAM. TCW 0x0809BE00 decodes (flycast core/hw/pvr/ta_structs.h union TCW: TexAddr:21, ScanOrder bit26, PixelFmt bits27-29) to: TexAddr=0x09BE00 -> VRAM BYTE 0x004DF000; PixelFmt=1 = Pixel565 (RGB565, 16bpp); ScanOrder=0 = TWIDDLED; VQ_Comp=0; non-palettized (NO palette bank — RGB565 carries colour directly). The 64KB region at 0x4DF000 decoded as RGB565 + Morton-detwiddle at 256x128 renders CLEAN readable HUD glyphs ("0123456789", "LEVEL", "TIME", "MAX", "WINS/LOSES", boxed digit grids, the circular meter gauge); the SAME bytes decoded LINEAR (no detwiddle) render as GARBLED COLOUR-NOISE = EXACTLY the live client symptom. So the garble = the client decoding the FONT texture WITHOUT the twiddle (or via the PAL4-only body path), NOT a wrong format/palette and NOT missing VRAM. The portrait/name region at 0x4EF000 (TCW 0x0809DE00/E000) is ALSO RGB565 TWIDDLED (renders char-name plates + portrait cells). CONFLICT RESOLVED: re_kb-27 source:hud_real_art_source called FONT.BIN rec1 "ARGB4444 twiddled" — that is the OFFLINE DISC-ASSET format; the ENGINE re-encodes/uploads it to VRAM as RGB565 twiddled. The LIVE VRAM + the live TCW (0x0809=fmt1) are the truth for the client decode; the disc format is irrelevant to the HUDQ path (which samples VRAM by tcw).';

UPSERT source:hud_font_tcw_setter SET kind='code',
  ref='marvelous2 bank0f loc_8C0F6044-loc_8C0F6056 (the HUD glyph poly record builder); #data loc_8C0F609C = 0x809',
  note='THE SET-SITE for the FONT/glyph HUD TCW (semantics come from where it is WRITTEN). The bank0f HUD-poly builder loads r3 = 0x809 (mov.w @(loc_8C0F609C,pc),r3) and stores it as the TCW HIGH word at record+0xCC (mov.w @(loc_8C0F609E,pc),r0 ; r0=0xCC ; mov.l r3,@(r0,r14)), while the TCW LOW half (TexAddr) is copied from the source record +0x48 (mov.l @(0x48,r13),r2 ; mov.l r2,@(0x48,r14)). So the engine HARD-SETS the upper TCW word = 0x0809 => PixelFmt=1 (RGB565), ScanOrder=0 (twiddled), non-VQ, non-palettized — CONFIRMING the live-captured TCW 0x0809BE00. FONT.BIN is file index 001 (build/data/filepnt.asm: #data filedic.loc_8c132adc ;001 FONT.BIN). The glyph poly is then handed to the cell processor bank12 loc_8C1294C8 (the record at r2+0x34) for emission into the surviving HUD pass.';

UPSERT finding:hud_font_glyph_decode_truth SET
  statement='THE GARBLE FIX (FONT glyph texture, ground-truthed): the in-match HUD FONT/digit/name glyphs at TCW 0x0809BE00 are RGB565, TWIDDLED (PVR/Morton), 16bpp, NON-PALETTIZED, residing at VRAM byte 0x004DF000 (TexAddr 0x09BE00<<3). The atlas region is 256x128 (64KB) for FONT and the portrait/name plates at 0x4EF000 (TCW 0x0809DE00/E000) are the same RGB565-twiddled family. PROOF (source:hud_font_vram_dump): the live prod VRAM at 0x4DF000 decoded RGB565+detwiddle at 256x128 = clean glyphs; decoded LINEAR (no twiddle) = garbled colour-noise == the exact live client symptom. ROOT CAUSE of the garble = the client samples this texture WITHOUT applying the twiddle (PVR ScanOrder=0), almost certainly because the render-replica pvr2 HUD path was only exercised on PAL4 body textures and does not honour a non-palettized RGB565 TWIDDLED sample for the HUD tcw. CONCRETE CLIENT DECODE the render-expert must apply for every textured HUD quad (pcw bit3==1): read tcw -> PixelFmt=(tcw>>27)&7 (==1 RGB565), ScanOrder=(tcw>>26)&1 (==0 -> TWIDDLE), VRAM byte = (tcw&0x1FFFFF)<<3; sample as RGB565 with Morton/PVR detwiddle (same _twiddleSlow lattice already in body_decoder.mjs, but RGB565 16bpp not PAL4); UV size from TSP (U=8<<((tsp>>3)&7), V=8<<(tsp&7)) — FONT is 256x128 (Usize=256 i.e. bits3-5=5, Vsize=128 i.e. bits0-2=4). Modulate by per-vertex col[i] (the team tint, already correct). The FONT VRAM IS in the shipped static prefix (maplecast_replica_live.cpp builds the full 8MB VRAM into the prefix at first armed in-match frame, AFTER match-load when the HUD textures are resident) — so no extra wire is needed; only the client decode must detwiddle RGB565.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

UPSERT finding:hudq_now_live_supersedes_empty SET
  statement='SUPERSEDES finding:hudq_empty_root_cause: as of 2026-06-14 the prod running binary IS the HUDQ build (md5 48364cd8d128de2b620ed749c2cb0a8d == the staged build) AND MAPLECAST_HUD_TA=1 is present in the RUNNING process env (/proc/PID/environ on 149.28.44.118 confirms it, wired via EnvironmentFile=-/etc/maplecast/headless.env which sets MAPLECAST_HUD_TA=1). So collectHudQuads runs, the HUDQ tail (magic 0x48554451) populates, and the client receives the engine REAL HUD quads — the garbled glyphs the user sees ARE the real engine FONT polys, decoded wrong client-side. The remaining work is therefore 100% client decode (finding:hud_font_glyph_decode_truth), NOT a server deploy/env gap. NOTE on QDIAG: arming MAPLECAST_QDIAG=1 for a one-shot HUD inventory did NOT produce /dev/shm/mc_hud_qdiag.log in a ~2min window even with active in-match ASMTRACE body output — the HUD-QDIAG branch (maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp:3300) requires the ctxv surviving-pass context which was not driving that capture path on this run; the VRAM dump settled format/twiddle/dims without it, so QDIAG was disarmed (restored to commented) after the run. OPEN if a byte-for-byte poly inventory is later needed: wire the HUD-QDIAG to the same ctx the live HUDQ tail uses, or read mc_oracle_hudQuads() counts directly.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

UPSERT finding:hud_meter_capture_completeness SET
  statement='SUPER-METER COMPOSITION + HUDQ CAPTURE COMPLETENESS. The real MVC2 hyper-combo gauge = a per-side numeric LEVEL glyph (FONT.BIN "LEVEL"+digit, the RGB565-twiddled glyphs at 0x4DF000 — the gauge labels "LEVEL"/"MAX" are VISIBLE in the decoded FONT dump), a SEGMENTED fill that retints per whole level, and notch separators, drawn outer-corner-inward (loc_8C0F0FDC METER_MAX=144; live fields meter_fill u16 0x8C289646 P1/0x8C289648 P2, meter_level u8 0x8C28964A P1/0x8C28964B P2). Each piece is its OWN HUD poly (a FONT-glyph quad for LEVEL/digit + white-texel modulated bars for the fill segments). collectHudQuads (maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp:2986) keeps polys by band+size: keep when (cy<HUD_TOPY=120 OR cy>=HUD_BOTY=420) AND NOT oversized (w<=320,h<=200) AND fmt!=7. The super meter sits in the LOWER corners (cy ~440-470 in 640x480) so it passes the BOTY band — its fill/segment quads ARE captured. RISK of dropped meter quads: (1) a meter/LEVEL glyph whose center cy lands in the MIDBAND 120..420 (e.g. a tall level-stack) is DROPPED (band=false) — the LEVEL number text and pips sit just above the bottom bar and could fall in the gap; (2) MAX_HUD cap (s_hud[MAX_HUD], sized from the 82-raw QDIAG busiest pass) — if a multi-level segmented gauge emits many small quads the cap could truncate; (3) the band cull was tuned on a low-meter capture, so high-meter (5-level) extra segment polys were likely NOT present when HUD_BOTY=420/MAX_HUD were calibrated. RECOMMENDED CAPTURE CHANGE (env-overridable, NO rebuild): widen the bottom band to catch the level labels by setting MAPLECAST_HUD_TA_BOTY lower (e.g. 400) and confirm MAX_HUD is not hit during a built-up-meter frame; a definitive inventory needs ONE QDIAG run captured during a 3+ level meter (the band/cap were derived from a low-meter pass). The exact dropped-quad list is OPEN pending that high-meter QDIAG capture.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='medium', date='2026-06-14';

UPSERT finding:hud_bar_team_tint_confirm SET
  statement='BAR/METER PER-TEAM TINT CONFIRMED. The life bars AND super-meter fill are NOT distinct sprites: they are WHITE-texel (or solid) polys MODULATED by a per-team-slot VERTEX COLOUR (bank15 loc_8c15FFB0, referenced from the in-match HUD dispatch bank0f loc_8C0F06E0). The HUDQ capture preserves this exactly: collectHudQuads stores the 4 per-vertex base colours (q.col[4], repacked to engine ARGB8888 from flycast vt.col[]) verbatim, and buildHudTA (replay.html) forces colType=0 packed-colour so col[i] drives the corners directly (replay.html:582-609). So the render-expert must MODULATE the bar/meter texel by the captured per-vertex col[i] (the bank15 magenta/green/cyan-per-active-point-char tint + dark-red red_health chip colour) — which the path already does for UNtextured quads; the FIX is only that TEXTURED HUD quads (the FONT glyphs) must ALSO be detwiddled-RGB565-sampled THEN modulated by col[i]. No extra tint logic is needed beyond honouring the captured col[4]; the engine already baked the per-team colour into the vertex colours, captured live.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

RELATE finding:hud_font_glyph_decode_truth->cites->source:hud_font_vram_dump;
RELATE finding:hud_font_glyph_decode_truth->cites->source:hud_font_tcw_setter;
