-- ============================================================================
-- 36c (2026-06-14): ENGINE HUD QUAD SUBMIT/WINDING ORDER re-grounded end-to-end
-- (the authoritative basis for the client strip order) + the two prior claims
-- reconciled with explicit CONFIRMED/REFUTED, cross-cited to disasm + flycast TA
-- parser + a LIVE 143-quad HUDQ capture rendered through pvr2. feat/render-replica-live.
-- ============================================================================

UPSERT source:hud_engine_submit_order SET kind='code',
  ref='marvelous2 bank0f loc_8C0F6044-loc_8C0F6056 (HUD glyph poly record builder) -> hands record r13+0x34 to bank12.loc_8c1294C8 (cell processor) which emits the PVR TA strip; flycast TA parser core/hw/pvr/ta_vtx.cpp: ta_poly_data L370-406 (walks Vertex_Parameter list, EndOfStrip terminates), vert_cvt_base_ L709-721 (vd_rc.verts.emplace_back per vertex, SUBMIT ORDER, NO reorder), EndPolyStrip L687-698 (PolyParam.first/.count span the contiguous submit run); makeIndex core/hw/pvr/ta_util.cpp L450-524 (strip->triangle index build, parity-duplicate preserves v0,v1,v2,v3 order). collectHudQuads core/network/maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp:3055-3066 stores vidx[0..3] = first 4 submit-order verts.',
  note='THE ENGINE HUD VERTEX/CORNER SUBMIT ORDER, ground truth for the client re-tile. The MVC2 HUD polys are PVR para TYPE 4 (Polygon, ListType 0 Opaque), Textured, StripLen=3 (max 4 verts) — CONFIRMED by decoding the LIVE-captured pcw 0x808c00xx from the 143-quad HUDQ tail: ParaType(bits29-31)=4, ListType(24-26)=0, Texture(bit3)=1, StripLen(bits18-19)=3 (NOT a type-5 Sprite). The engine submits each HUD poly as a 4-vertex PVR TRIANGLE STRIP (v0,v1,v2,v3). flycast ta_vtx.cpp appends each strip vertex to vd_rc.verts in pure submit order (vert_cvt_base_ emplace_back, no permutation); EndPolyStrip records PolyParam.first/.count over that contiguous run. collectHudQuads captures vidx[0..3] = exactly those first 4 submit-order verts. The hardware strip rule for a 4-vert strip is the IDENTITY: verts (0,1,2,3) tessellate to triangles (0,1,2)+(1,2,3) with the shared diagonal between v1 and v2. THEREFORE the correct client re-tile is the IDENTITY strip [0,1,2,3] (the engine`s own two triangles), NOT a perimeter-walk [0,1,3,2]. This CONFIRMS the render-expert`s [0,1,2,3] fix. PROOF (live, rendered through the real pvr2 path, _hud_cap/names_zoom_{0123,0132}.png): [0,1,2,3] -> readable "TIME"/"LEVEL"/digits + clean bars; [0,1,3,2] -> diagonally mis-tiled glyph-slice noise == the exact live garble symptom. The corner coords confirm strips, not bbox: e.g. quad[1] x=[33,33,36,36] y=[67,49,69,46] is an angled italic parallelogram (top/bottom edges sheared), so a bbox or wrong-diagonal tiling shears every glyph.';

UPSERT finding:hud_engine_submit_winding_confirmed SET
  statement='ENGINE HUD QUAD SUBMIT/WINDING ORDER = a 4-vertex PVR triangle STRIP in native submit order (v0,v1,v2,v3) -> hardware triangles (0,1,2)+(1,2,3); the correct client re-tile is the IDENTITY strip [0,1,2,3]. GROUNDING: (1) PVR para type 4 Polygon / ListType 0 Opaque / StripLen 3 / Textured, decoded from the LIVE HUDQ pcw 0x808c00xx (143-quad capture, source:hudq_live_capture_2026_06_14) — NOT a type-5 Sprite, so it is a real strip whose corner order is meaningful. (2) flycast`s TA parser preserves submit order with ZERO reordering (ta_vtx.cpp vert_cvt_base_ emplace_back per vertex; EndPolyStrip spans PolyParam.first/.count over the contiguous run; makeIndex parity-duplication preserves v0..v3), so collectHudQuads vidx[0..3] (maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp:3055) ARE the engine`s own submit-order corners. (3) The bank0f HUD poly builder (loc_8C0F6044) hands the record to the bank12 cell processor (loc_8c1294C8) which emits that strip. (4) EMPIRICAL: rendering the captured corners as [0,1,2,3] through the real pvr2 path yields readable HUD; [0,1,3,2] yields the live garble (_hud_cap/names_zoom_*.png). So the engine order IS the identity strip and [0,1,2,3] is CONFIRMED correct. The captured corners are angled parallelograms (sheared italic glyphs), which is why the wrong diagonal ([0,1,3,2]) shears each glyph into colour-noise rather than just flipping a quad.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

UPSERT finding:hud_prior_detwiddle_claim_refuted SET
  statement='RECONCILE / RETRACTION of two prior conflicting claims. CLAIM A (a prior mvc2-sh4-re-expert run): "the pvr2 HUD path is not detwiddling RGB565 twiddled, so the client decodes the FONT texture wrong." THIS IS REFUTED. It was an INFERENCE about CLIENT code the prior run never read; the client DOES apply the Morton/PVR detwiddle for RGB565 twiddled (the render-expert verified texture-manager.mjs:172 `scan===0 ? <linear> : twop(x,y,bx,by)` — twop is the twiddle path, taken when ScanOrder==0). The font DECODE is correct: the SAME bytes from LIVE prod VRAM 0x4DF000 (TCW 0x0809BE00) decoded RGB565+detwiddle yield clean readable glyphs (source:hud_font_vram_dump, /dev/shm/mc_vram_dump.bin, re-confirmed 2026-06-14: twiddled=readable "0123456/LEVEL/TIME/MAX/WINS/LOSES"+gauge; linear=colour-noise). NOTE: an earlier note in THIS file (finding:hud_font_glyph_decode_truth) also leaned toward "client samples without the twiddle" as the root cause — that too is now SUPERSEDED by the strip-order finding; the twiddle decode was already correct client-side. CLAIM B (the real cause): "the garble is the TRIANGLE-STRIP CORNER ORDER in the client re-tile (buildHudTA defaulting to [0,1,3,2] instead of the engine`s identity strip [0,1,2,3])." THIS IS CONFIRMED — by the engine submit order being a native 4-vert strip (finding:hud_engine_submit_winding_confirmed) AND the live render proof that [0,1,2,3] reads clean while [0,1,3,2] garbles. ONE RECONCILED TRUTH: decode (format=RGB565, scan=twiddled, dims, palette, VRAM presence) is correct on BOTH engine and client; the garble was the strip-order re-tile, now fixed to the engine`s identity [0,1,2,3].',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

RELATE finding:hud_engine_submit_winding_confirmed->cites->source:hud_engine_submit_order;
RELATE finding:hud_engine_submit_winding_confirmed->cites->source:hudq_live_capture_2026_06_14;
RELATE finding:hud_engine_submit_winding_confirmed->cites->source:hud_render_routine_rom;
RELATE finding:hud_engine_submit_winding_confirmed->about->finding:hud_font_garble_strip_order;
RELATE finding:hud_prior_detwiddle_claim_refuted->cites->source:hud_font_vram_dump;
RELATE finding:hud_prior_detwiddle_claim_refuted->about->finding:hud_engine_submit_winding_confirmed;
RELATE finding:hud_prior_detwiddle_claim_refuted->about->finding:hud_font_glyph_decode_truth;

-- ============================================================================
-- 36d (2026-06-14): INDEPENDENT CLIENT-SIDE re-grounding by the render-pipeline
-- expert. The 36c grounding leaned on the C++ flycast TA parser (the SERVER-side
-- capture); this pins the CLIENT-side triangulation that ACTUALLY draws the
-- captured corners (pvr2-renderer.mjs), plus a fresh live pixel-diff. Closes the
-- chain end-to-end on the code the browser runs. feat/render-replica-live.
-- ============================================================================

UPSERT source:hud_client_retile_pvr2 SET kind='code',
  ref='web/webgpu/pvr2-renderer.mjs _buildIndexBuffer (grep the name; was ~L142-164); web/render-replica/replay.html buildHudTA (grep; was ~L571-619, order default [0,1,2,3] @ the `order =` line); core/network/maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp collectHudQuads (grep; storage loop ~L3055-3066); core/hw/pvr/ta_vtx.cpp vert_cvt_base_ (emplace_back per vertex) + glob_param_bdc_ (d_pp->first = verts.size()) + EndPolyStrip (count = verts.size()-first); web/webgpu/texture-manager.mjs _decode (idx = scan===1 ? linear : twop(...)).',
  note='THE CLIENT DRAW PATH, ground-truthed on the code the BROWSER runs (the 36c grounding cited the C++ parser; this is the JS that re-tiles the captured corners). CHAIN, each link cited: (1) CAPTURE STORES SUBMIT ORDER — collectHudQuads walks k=pp.first..pp.first+pp.count over rc.idx[k] (or rc.verts directly for autosort tr), takes the first 4 into vidx[nv++], then copies vidx[c] straight into q.x[c]/y[c]/u[c]/v[c]/col[c] with NO reorder; the C++ verts were appended in pure TA submit order (ta_vtx.cpp vert_cvt_base_ emplace_back; pp.first/.count span that contiguous run). => q.x[0..3] ARE engine strip verts V0,V1,V2,V3. (2) CLIENT RE-TILES AS A STRIP IN ARRAY ORDER — pvr2-renderer.mjs _buildIndexBuffer triangulates a count-vertex PolyParam as a GPU triangle strip from pp.first: for i in 0..count-2, even i -> (v0,v1,v2), odd i -> (v1,v0,v2) [winding-flip]; for count=4 this is triangles (V0,V1,V2)+(V2,V1,V3) == the hardware strip (0,1,2)+(1,2,3). It consumes the 4 verts in the ORDER THEY SIT IN THE ARRAY. (3) buildHudTA writes the 4 corners into that array in order[k] sequence; identity order=[0,1,2,3] feeds V0,V1,V2,V3 back in their captured submit order => reproduces the engine`s OWN two triangles byte-for-byte. order=[0,1,3,2] swaps V2<->V3 => strip triangles (0,1,3)+(3,1,2), a bowtie/wrong-diagonal mis-tile of each sheared italic glyph slice = the garble. (4) DECODE IS CORRECT — texture-manager.mjs _decode: `const idx = scan===1 ? y*w+x : twop(x,y,bx,by)`; FONT tcw 0x0809BE00 has ScanOrder bit26=0 => twop (Morton detwiddle) IS applied; fmt=1 => u565 RGB565. CONFIRMED by reading the exact line. So [0,1,2,3] is PROVEN from source (capture-order + client strip triangulation + identity re-tile), independent of "it looked readable".';

UPSERT source:hud_pixel_diff_2026_06_14 SET kind='oracle',
  ref='node tools/render-replica-poc/hudq_capture.mjs --url wss://nobd.net/replica-live --frames 400 --want-hud 30 (saved _hud_cap_def/{vram_prefix.bin 8MB, pvr_prefix.bin 32KB, hudq_tail.bin 104 quads}); rendered via tools/render-replica-poc/render_hudq.mjs (Dawn/webgpu, pvr2-renderer+texture-manager+ta-parser VERBATIM) at --order 0,1,2,3 vs 0,1,3,2; FONT atlas ground-truthed via tools/render-replica-poc/_decode_font2.mjs (TextureManager._decode, fmt=1 RGB565 scan=0, VRAM 0x4DF000, 256x128).',
  note='FRESH LIVE PIXEL-DIFF PROOF (render-pipeline expert, independent of the 36c capture). Live capture: 104 HUD quads/frame. FONT GROUND TRUTH: _decode_font2.mjs decoded VRAM 0x4DF000 via the REAL client TextureManager._decode (RGB565, scan=0 twiddled) -> font_atlas_gt.png shows CLEAN readable glyph atlas ("TIME" yellow, "SENTINEL"/"LEVEL"/"MAX"/digit grids, the circular meter gauge), glyphs stored mirror-imaged (the FONT quads carry mirrored UVs u 0.996->0.754 to flip them upright) -> a non-detwiddled decode would be Morton-noise, so the decode/twiddle is CONFIRMED correct. RENDER DIFF (P1bigname.png / P2bigname.png, top=[0,1,2,3] FIX, bottom=[0,1,3,2] OLD): FIX -> clean upright white glyphs ("NEL" tail of SENTINEL, "BLE" tail of CABLE) + clean red/yellow meter bars; OLD -> same glyph rows sheared + the meter bars show a DIAGONAL colour wedge/gradient-bleed (the bar quad`s two triangles tiled across the wrong diagonal, dragging the gouraud corner-to-corner) == the live garble symptom. NOTE on what the FONT.BIN 0x4DF000 region actually carries: the tcw=0x0809BE00 HUD quads are the angled FRAME/underline STROKES of the name plates (w=225 h=2, w=3 h=23 parallelograms with sheared corners e.g. y=[67,49,69,46]); the per-CHARACTER big-name letters are the fmt=5 PAL4 quads in the 0x445000+ bank (one tcw per glyph). BOTH families are 4-vert strips and BOTH are fixed by the identity re-tile. The control word confirms a real strip: live pcw 0x808c003e decodes ParaType=4 (Polygon), ListType=0 (Opaque), StripLen=3 (4 verts/2 tris), Texture=1, Gouraud=1 -> NOT a type-5 Sprite, so corner order is load-bearing.';

UPSERT finding:hud_garble_one_truth_clientgrounded SET
  statement='ONE GROUNDED TRUTH (render-pipeline expert, client-code-cited, pixel-proven). The HUD FONT/name garble was the CLIENT TRIANGLE-STRIP RE-TILE ORDER, NOT the texture decode. PROOF CHAIN (every link a read source line): (a) collectHudQuads stores the 4 corners in engine TA SUBMIT order with no reorder (oracle_hook.cpp collectHudQuads, vidx[c]->q.x[c]); (b) those C++ verts were appended in submit order (ta_vtx.cpp vert_cvt_base_ emplace_back; first/count span the run); (c) the CLIENT pvr2-renderer.mjs _buildIndexBuffer triangulates a PolyParam as a strip over pp.first..first+count IN ARRAY ORDER (even i->(v0,v1,v2), odd i->(v1,v0,v2)); (d) buildHudTA (replay.html) writes corners in order[k]; identity [0,1,2,3] => reproduces the engine strip (0,1,2)+(1,2,3); [0,1,3,2] => wrong diagonal => garble; (e) the live pcw 0x808c003e is ParaType=4/StripLen=3 (a real 4-vert strip, NOT a sprite) so the order matters; (f) DECODE is correct — texture-manager.mjs _decode applies twop (detwiddle) for scan=0, and the live VRAM 0x4DF000 decoded via the real TextureManager._decode yields clean glyphs (font_atlas_gt.png). PIXEL DIFF (source:hud_pixel_diff_2026_06_14): [0,1,2,3] clean / [0,1,3,2] diagonal-sheared bars+glyphs. RECONCILIATION (explicit): CLAIM "RGB565 not detwiddled" = REFUTED (texture-manager.mjs _decode line `scan===1 ? y*w+x : twop(x,y,bx,by)` applies the detwiddle for the FONT scan=0; glyphs decode clean). CLAIM "wrong triangle-strip order [0,1,3,2]->[0,1,2,3]" = CONFIRMED (capture-order + client strip triangulation + the live pixel diff). The fix is ALREADY deployed in replay.html buildHudTA (commit 52892ced1, order default [0,1,2,3]); this finding RE-GROUNDS that justification on the client code + a fresh live diff, replacing the earlier "engine native submit order" assertion with the cited capture->triangulate->retile chain. NO residual client bug remains for the strip path: [0,1,2,3] is correct for ALL HUD strips (FONT-frame, PAL4 glyphs, bars). Independent open items (NOT the garble, tracked elsewhere): the fmt=5 PAL4 meter art VRAM coverage (finding:hud_meter_segments_vram_gap) is a SERVER prefix gap; multi-glyph tier-2 name plates are a fidelity refinement.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

RELATE finding:hud_garble_one_truth_clientgrounded->cites->source:hud_client_retile_pvr2;
RELATE finding:hud_garble_one_truth_clientgrounded->cites->source:hud_pixel_diff_2026_06_14;
RELATE finding:hud_garble_one_truth_clientgrounded->about->finding:hud_engine_submit_winding_confirmed;
RELATE finding:hud_garble_one_truth_clientgrounded->about->finding:hud_prior_detwiddle_claim_refuted;
RELATE finding:hud_garble_one_truth_clientgrounded->about->finding:hud_font_garble_strip_order;

-- ============================================================================
-- 36e (2026-06-14): THE BIG-NAME GARBLE ROOT CAUSE = ParaType-5 PVR SPRITES,
-- not a server VRAM gap and not the [0,1,2,3] strip order. The "missing VRAM"
-- hypothesis (names are PAL4 art in the 0x440000-0x460000 ZEROED prefix block)
-- is REFUTED by a FRESH LIVE CAPTURE: the texels AND palette ARE shipped; the
-- garble reproduces through the verbatim pvr2 path with the present data, and
-- isolates to the engine's ParaType-5 Sprite vertex layout. feat/render-replica-live.
-- ============================================================================

UPSERT source:hud_name_sprite_live_capture_2026_06_14b SET kind='oracle',
  ref='node tools/render-replica-poc/hudq_capture.mjs --url wss://nobd.net/replica-live --outdir _hud_cap_namegap (FRESH live session, vframe 86530, 114 quads; saved vram_prefix.bin 8MB + pvr_prefix.bin 32KB + hudq_tail.bin + hudq_inventory.txt). Analyzed: tools/render-replica-poc/_name_vram_probe.mjs (tcw->VRAM addr + 64KB-block histogram + palette-bank non-zero). Rendered VERBATIM through pvr2: tools/render-replica-poc/render_hudq.mjs (Dawn D3D12, pvr2-renderer+texture-manager+ta-parser).',
  note='FRESH LIVE PROD CAPTURE (current session, NOT a reused good capture). HUDQ ACTIVE: 114 quads/frame (window.__hudQuadCount>0 equivalent — the tail is populated). QUAD CENSUS by ParaType x fmt (pcw bits29-31): para4_fmt1=43 (FONT frame/underline strokes, tcw 0809BE00), para4_fmt2=9 (portrait/icon, tcw 0809DE/DF/E0 + 1009CE00 + 5008F700), para5_fmt5=62 (the BIG-NAME letters, PAL4, tcw 2A.../2B...). ALL 62 fmt=5 quads are ParaType=5 (Sprite), span screen x20..620 y73..104 (the name-plate band, 41 of them at y~80). VRAM COVERAGE (64KB-block non-zero histogram on the SHIPPED prefix): the name sprites reference VRAM 0x415400..0x41d000 (tcw&0x1FFFFF<<3), all inside the 0x410000 block which is 53.0% non-zero = POPULATED (NOT zero). The only fully-ZERO blocks in 0x400000..0x480000 are 0x430000 and 0x460000 and NO HUD quad references either. PALETTE COVERAGE (pvr_prefix PALETTE_RAM @0x1000): the name sprites use palSel banks 16/17/24 ((tcw>>21)&0x3F); each bank is 15/16 non-zero (index0=transparent) = POPULATED + correct. So texels AND palette ARE shipped for the names.';

UPSERT source:hud_sprite_expand_flycast SET kind='code',
  ref='core/hw/pvr/ta_vtx.cpp AppendSpriteParam (grep; was ~L1010), AppendSpriteVertexA (~L1047), AppendSpriteVertexB (~L1124), CaclulateSpritePlane (~L1075); ParamType_Sprite dispatch (~L522). core/network/maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp collectHudQuads (vidx[0..3]=first 4 rc.verts in array order). web/render-replica/replay.html buildHudTA (rewrites pcw=(4<<29)|(2<<24)|low24, re-tiles order default [0,1,2,3]).',
  note='THE FLYCAST PVR-SPRITE (ParaType 5) VERTEX EXPANSION — why a sprite is NOT a polygon strip. A PVR Sprite submits 3 explicit XYZ corners + 4 UVs and the hardware DERIVES the 4th corner + its UV from the plane. flycast AppendSpriteVertexA/B lays the 4 expanded verts into rc.verts in this GEOMETRIC order: cv[2]=(x0,y0,z0)/uv(u0,v0); cv[3]=(x1,y1,z1)/uv(u1,v1); cv[1]=(x2,y2,z2)/uv(u2,v2); cv[0]=(x3,y3) with z,u,v COMPUTED by CaclulateSpritePlane (P.u=A_u+k1*AB_u+k2*AC_u — a plane interpolation, NOT a stored UV). So the verts array order is [P, corner2, corner0, corner1] and slot 0 carries an INTERPOLATED UV valid only for flycast`s own sprite rasterization. collectHudQuads grabs vidx[0..3]=first 4 rc.verts in array order with NO sprite/polygon distinction, stores the original ParaType-5 pcw. The client buildHudTA then FORCES pcw para=4 (polygon) and re-tiles as an identity triangle strip [0,1,2,3] over {P,c2,c0,c1} => triangles (P,c2,c0)+(c2,c0,c1): wrong diagonal AND a plane-interpolated UV at a real corner => the name sprites shear into PAL4 colour-noise. This is DISTINCT from the FONT (para=4) garble (36c/36d) which WAS the [0,1,3,2]->[0,1,2,3] strip-order fix; para=4 polys ARE real strips and [0,1,2,3] is correct for them.';

UPSERT finding:hud_name_garble_is_paratype5_sprite SET
  statement='THE BIG-NAME GARBLE = ParaType-5 PVR SPRITES mishandled as polygons CLIENT-SIDE, NOT a server VRAM-coverage gap. The "names are PAL4 art in the 0x440000-0x460000 ZEROED prefix block" hypothesis (the twin of finding:hud_meter_segments_vram_gap) is REFUTED by a fresh live capture (source:hud_name_sprite_live_capture_2026_06_14b): the per-character big-name letters are 62 fmt=5 PAL4 quads at VRAM 0x415400..0x41d000 (block 0x410000 = 53% non-zero, POPULATED) using palette banks 16/17/24 (15/16 non-zero, POPULATED) — texels AND palette ARE in the shipped prefix. The garble REPRODUCES through the verbatim pvr2 path (render_hudq.mjs) with that present data, at BOTH strip orders [0,1,2,3] AND [0,1,3,2] (both diagonal-sheared blue/yellow streaks), while the para=4 polygon quads (portraits, bars, FONT-frame strokes) in the SAME capture render CLEAN (readable portrait faces, red bars, partial "BLE"/"INEL"/"RM" frame text) — isolating the bug to the 62 ParaType-5 sprites. ROOT CAUSE (source:hud_sprite_expand_flycast): all 62 name quads carry pcw a2000009 => ParaType(bits29-31)=5 (Sprite). flycast`s sprite expansion (ta_vtx.cpp AppendSpriteVertexA/B + CaclulateSpritePlane) lays the 4 verts into rc.verts in GEOMETRIC order [P, corner2, corner0, corner1] where slot0=P has a PLANE-INTERPOLATED UV (not a stored corner UV). collectHudQuads captures those 4 verts in array order with no sprite distinction; buildHudTA rewrites pcw to para=4 polygon and re-tiles as an identity strip [0,1,2,3] => triangles over the wrong diagonal with an interpolated UV at a corner => sheared PAL4 noise. The [0,1,2,3] fix (finding:hud_garble_one_truth_clientgrounded) is correct for the FONT/portrait/bar PARA=4 polys but DOES NOT (and cannot) fix the PARA=5 sprites — confirming the user`s report that names still garble identically after the strip fix shipped. NO single static corner-reorder ([2,3,1,0]/[2,0,1,3]/[2,3,0,1] all tested) fixes it because slot0`s UV is interpolated; the sprite must be handled AS a sprite. FIX DOMAIN = CLIENT (not server): either (a) at capture, detect ParaType-5 and store the THREE explicit sprite corners + UVs + derive the 4th the engine`s way (a sprite-aware HudQuad), then re-tile as the real sprite quad; or (b) keep the 4 expanded verts but mark them sprite-derived and re-tile in the flycast geometric order [P,c2,c0,c1] with the plane-derived UV preserved (NOT rewritten to a polygon). The server prefix already ships everything needed (texels + palette); no maplecast_replica_live.cpp change is required for the names. SUPERSEDES the parenthetical in finding:hud_garble_one_truth_clientgrounded that "[0,1,2,3] is correct for ALL HUD strips (FONT-frame, PAL4 glyphs, bars)" — it is correct for the para=4 polys only; the PAL4 NAME glyphs are para=5 sprites and need sprite handling. ALSO CORRECTS the finding:hud_meter_segments_vram_gap / finding:hud_garble_one_truth_clientgrounded note that names live at ~0x445000 in the 0x440000-0x460000 zeroed block: in THIS live session the name sprites are at 0x415xxx-0x41dxxx (populated). (The 0x440000/0x450000 blocks are 27.7%/29.7% non-zero — NOT 100% zero either; the meter-segment VRAM-gap claim itself should be re-verified against a live high-meter capture before any server change.)',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

UPSERT finding:hud_name_palette_coverage_ok SET
  statement='PAL4 HUD-NAME PALETTE BANK COVERAGE = SHIPPED + CORRECT (task-3 check, REFUTES a missing-palette alternate cause). The fmt=5 PAL4 name sprites use palSel banks 16 (P1C1), 17, and 24 (P2C1) ((tcw>>21)&0x3F from tcw 2A.../2B...). In the FRESH live prefix pvr_prefix.bin PALETTE_RAM (pvr_regs+0x1000, bank b at off 0x1000+b*16*4), bank 16 = 15/16 non-zero (first entries 0,0xf78d,0xf459,0xf237 ARGB4444 in the low 16 bits), bank 17 = 15/16 non-zero (0,0xffff,0xfbff,0xf8ef), bank 24 = 15/16 non-zero (0,0xfc7d,0xf849,0xf627) — index0=transparent, 15 real colours each. So the HUD-name PAL4 palette IS covered by the once-shipped prefix pvr_regs block (and the on-change palette tail, cpp:215-247 pvrPalSig + the FRMx palette tail, would refresh it on any post-prefix write). A missing HUD-font palette is NOT the cause; the garble is purely the ParaType-5 sprite re-tile (finding:hud_name_garble_is_paratype5_sprite).',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

RELATE finding:hud_name_garble_is_paratype5_sprite->cites->source:hud_name_sprite_live_capture_2026_06_14b;
RELATE finding:hud_name_garble_is_paratype5_sprite->cites->source:hud_sprite_expand_flycast;
RELATE finding:hud_name_garble_is_paratype5_sprite->about->finding:hud_garble_one_truth_clientgrounded;
RELATE finding:hud_name_garble_is_paratype5_sprite->about->finding:hud_meter_segments_vram_gap;
RELATE finding:hud_name_palette_coverage_ok->cites->source:hud_name_sprite_live_capture_2026_06_14b;
RELATE finding:hud_name_palette_coverage_ok->about->finding:replica_live_palette_gap;

-- ============================================================================
-- 36g (2026-06-14): THE SPRITE-AWARE RE-TILE FIX IMPLEMENTED + PROVEN on the
-- reproducing capture (_hud_cap_namegap), by the mvc2-sprite-render expert (owns
-- buildHudTA). Implements 36f's recipe AND uncovers a SECOND, server-side root
-- cause: collectHudQuads MIS-CAPTURES ~half the name sprites' verts (autosort-tr
-- rc.idx aliasing) -> a server change is required for the LEADING letters. The
-- client fix removes the garble STREAKS now; the server fix completes the names.
-- feat/render-replica-live.
-- ============================================================================

UPSERT source:hud_sprite_fix_render_2026_06_14 SET kind='oracle',
  ref='tools/render-replica-poc/_spr_probe.mjs + _prove_replay.mjs (extracts buildHudTA VERBATIM from web/render-replica/replay.html, renders via the verbatim pvr2 path Dawn/D3D12) on tools/render-replica-poc/_hud_cap_namegap/ (live capture vframe 86530, 114 quads, 62 fmt=5 sprites). BEFORE/AFTER: _PROOF_replay_before_after.png. Degeneracy census: tools/render-replica-poc (inline). Server-fix grounding: core/hw/pvr/ta_util.cpp sortTriangles L66-185.',
  note='IMPLEMENTATION + PIXEL PROOF of the ParaType-5 sprite re-tile, rendered through replay.html`s OWN extracted buildHudTA. AFTER (sprite-aware order + degenerate guard): the diagonal blue/yellow GARBLE STREAKS are GONE and the name letters read clean white italic — left CABLE("3LE")/SENTINEL("INEL")/STORM("TRM"), right CABLE x3 ("3LE"). BEFORE (para5 coerced to para4 identity, the shipped pre-fix behavior): the same name rows streak into blue (left) + yellow/orange (right) diagonal wedges == the live user symptom. The para=4 polys (portraits/bars/FONT-frame strokes) are UNCHANGED and stay clean. DEGENERACY CENSUS of the 62 captured fmt=5 sprites (this capture): 16 clean parallelograms, 15 "wide" (>40px span, verts split across two far-apart x-clusters = TWO glyphs merged), 31 with duplicate/collapsed corners. So 46/62 captured sprite quads are NOT a single valid sprite — they streak under ANY winding and the client GUARD (_hudSpriteUsable) drops them (272 verts kept vs 456 = 68 of 114 quads drawn). The 16 clean + the guard => the trailing letters render correctly with zero streaks; the LEADING letters are the dropped mis-captured sprites.';

UPSERT finding:hud_sprite_capture_server_bug SET
  statement='SECOND ROOT CAUSE (NEW, server-side): collectHudQuads MIS-CAPTURES ~46/62 HUD name-sprite quads because it reads the 4 corners via rc.idx in an AUTOSORT-TRANSLUCENT pass. ta_util.cpp sortTriangles (L66-185) does NOT rewrite pp.first for tr polys (it stays a rc.verts offset) but APPENDS depth-sorted triangle indices to rc.idx starting at idxSize; so collectHudQuads` primary walk rc.idx[pp.first..pp.first+count] indexes the SORTED idx array at the wrong place and grabs verts belonging to OTHER polys -> the captured quad merges two adjacent glyphs (verts split across two x-clusters, e.g. quad[41] x=[48,201,200,209]) or collapses corners (duplicate verts / zero UV, e.g. quad[64] 3 verts uv=0,0). This SUPERSEDES re_kb 36f`s premise that "the 4 captured verts ARE flycast`s expanded sprite verts" — true for only ~16/62; the rest are corrupt. EMPIRICAL: standalone-decoding any single name sprite`s tile is noise (expected — thin UV sub-slice), but the per-sprite SCREEN GEOMETRY is provably wrong (two x-clusters in one quad). THE SPRITE VERTS ARE CONTIGUOUS at rc.verts[pp.first..pp.first+4] (AppendSpriteVertexA/B write them there) in BOTH autosort and non-autosort, so the fix is to read them DIRECTLY for ParaType-5. SERVER FIX IMPLEMENTED (maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp collectHudQuads): detect isSpritePara=((pcw>>29)&7)==5 and force the rc.verts-direct read (the existing seen==0 fallback path) instead of the rc.idx walk. NEEDS A REBUILD + DEPLOY of the headless binary (the current _hud_cap_namegap capture was made with the BUGGY server, so the leading letters cannot be recovered from it offline). After deploy + a fresh capture, the client guard will pass all (now-clean) sprites and the FULL names spell out.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

UPSERT finding:hud_sprite_client_fix_shipped SET
  statement='CLIENT FIX SHIPPED (buildHudTA, web/render-replica/replay.html) implementing re_kb 36f`s recipe + a degenerate guard. For a captured quad whose pcw ParaType (bits29-31)==5 (PVR Sprite, the name letters): (1) _hudSpriteUsable(q) drops mis-captured quads (x-span>48px = merged glyphs, OR <4 distinct corners, OR <3 distinct UVs) so they cannot streak (overridable via window._hudSpriteNoGuard); (2) _hudSpriteOrder(q) re-tiles the survivors as a CONVEX QUAD along the true diagonal: sort the 4 corners by centroid angle -> pm[], emit strip [pm1,pm0,pm2,pm3] so pvr2 _buildIndexBuffer draws tris (pm1,pm0,pm2)+(pm0,pm2,pm3) (diagonal pm0-pm2), each vert keeping its CAPTURED u/v/col (P keeps its plane UV). ParaType-4 polys KEEP the identity strip [0,1,2,3] (correct, finding:hud_garble_one_truth_clientgrounded) and window._hudQuadOrder still overrides them. PROVEN on the reproducing capture (source:hud_sprite_fix_render_2026_06_14, _PROOF_replay_before_after.png) rendered through replay.html`s OWN buildHudTA: streaks gone, trailing name letters readable + correctly spelled. This is the FULL fix the client can deliver on the buggy-capture data; the LEADING letters need the server capture fix (finding:hud_sprite_capture_server_bug). Title build tag bumped hud:ui2-stripfix -> hud:ui2-spritefix.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

RELATE finding:hud_sprite_client_fix_shipped->cites->source:hud_sprite_fix_render_2026_06_14;
RELATE finding:hud_sprite_client_fix_shipped->cites->source:hud_sprite_expand_recipe;
RELATE finding:hud_sprite_client_fix_shipped->about->finding:hud_sprite_paratype5_client_recipe;
RELATE finding:hud_sprite_client_fix_shipped->about->finding:hud_name_garble_is_paratype5_sprite;
RELATE finding:hud_sprite_capture_server_bug->cites->source:hud_sprite_fix_render_2026_06_14;
RELATE finding:hud_sprite_capture_server_bug->about->finding:hud_sprite_paratype5_client_recipe;
RELATE finding:hud_sprite_capture_server_bug->about->finding:hud_name_letters_render_confirmed;

-- ============================================================================
-- 36h (2026-06-14): THE CENTROID/ATAN2 HEURISTIC REPLACED BY THE ENGINE'S EXACT
-- TRIANGULATION. The user rejected geometric inference: no centroid sort, no
-- perimeter atan2. Grounded END-TO-END in engine source (ta_vtx.cpp expansion +
-- ta_util.cpp strip triangulation) that the IDENTITY strip [0,1,2,3] over the
-- raw expansion order [P,C,A,B] IS the engine's own two triangles, so the
-- heuristic was unnecessary AND wrong. feat/render-replica-live.
-- ============================================================================

UPSERT source:hud_sprite_expand_engine_order SET kind='code',
  ref='core/hw/pvr/ta_vtx.cpp AppendSpriteVertexA (L1047-1073) + AppendSpriteVertexB (L1124-1153) + CaclulateSpritePlane (L1075-1122); core/hw/pvr/ta_util.cpp sortTriangles (L84-130, the strip-walk); web/webgpu/pvr2-renderer.mjs _buildIndexBuffer (L156-160); core/network/maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp collectHudQuads (isSpritePara rc.verts-direct read, L3025-3047).',
  note='THE ENGINE SPRITE TRIANGULATION, READ FROM SOURCE (proves the identity strip, no heuristic). ta_vtx.cpp lays the 4 expanded sprite verts CONTIGUOUSLY at rc.verts[pp.first..+4] in the FIXED order cv=[P,C,A,B]: AppendSpriteVertexA sets cv[2]=(x0,y0,z0), cv[3]=(x1,y1,z1), cv[1].x=x2; AppendSpriteVertexB sets cv[1].y/z=(y2,z2), cv[0].x/y=(x3,y3), uv: sprite_uv(2,u0,v0) sprite_uv(3,u1,v1) sprite_uv(1,u2,v2), then CaclulateSpritePlane(cv) fills cv[0]=P with PLANE-INTERPOLATED z/u/v (P.u=A_u+k1*AB_u+k2*AC_u, A=cv[2],B=cv[3],C=cv[1],P=cv[0]). So array order = [P(cv0), C(cv1), A(cv2), B(cv3)]. ta_util.cpp sortTriangles walks that strip: v0=cv0=P, v1=cv1=C; i=2 -> v2=cv2=A -> tri (P,C,A), even i so v0:=A; i=3 -> v2=cv3=B -> tri (A,C,B) (v0=A,v1=C,v2=B). The ACTUALLY-DRAWN triangles are (P,C,A)+(A,C,B), shared diagonal C-A. The CLIENT pvr2-renderer.mjs _buildIndexBuffer triangulates a count-vert strip over pp.first IN ARRAY ORDER (even i->(v0,v1,v2), odd i->(v1,v0,v2)); fed [P,C,A,B] it emits (P,C,A)+(A,C,B) == byte-identical to sortTriangles. The SERVER collectHudQuads captures sprites via rc.verts[pp.first..+4] DIRECTLY (isSpritePara, NOT the depth-sorted/re-indexed rc.idx), so q.x/y/u/v/col[0..3] ARE [P,C,A,B] raw. THEREFORE the identity [0,1,2,3] re-tile reproduces the engine exactly — the centroid/atan2 perimeter sort was a geometric reconstruction of the rc.idx permutation that raw-order capture eliminates at the source. No sprite-specific re-tile, no guard needed once capture is raw-order.';

UPSERT finding:hud_sprite_engine_order_replaces_heuristic SET
  statement='SUPERSEDES finding:hud_sprite_client_fix_shipped: the centroid/atan2 perimeter sort (_hudSpriteOrder) + degenerate guard (_hudSpriteUsable) are REMOVED from buildHudTA (web/render-replica/replay.html). ParaType-5 sprites now use the SAME identity strip [0,1,2,3] as ParaType-4 polys, because the IDENTITY order over the raw expansion order [P,C,A,B] IS the engine\'s own triangulation (source:hud_sprite_expand_engine_order: ta_vtx.cpp expansion + ta_util.cpp sortTriangles -> tris (P,C,A)+(A,C,B); pvr2-renderer.mjs _buildIndexBuffer reproduces them from the identity array). The PREREQUISITE is that the SERVER captures sprites in raw expansion order, which collectHudQuads ALREADY does (isSpritePara -> rc.verts[pp.first..+4] direct, committed 6b28bac21; the prior rc.idx walk was the permutation that drove the heuristic). NO geometric inference is used — the order comes from the engine\'s data. VALIDATION (tools/render-replica-poc/_validate_engineorder.mjs, on _hud_cap_namegap vframe 86530, rendered through the verbatim pvr2 path): the 16 cleanly-captured trailing letters ("INEL"/SENTINEL, "TRM"/STORM, "3LE"/CABLE x multiple) render IDENTICALLY under BEFORE(centroid+guard) and AFTER(identity) — proving the identity order is correct for validly-captured sprites with no sort. CAVEAT: that capture was made with the OLD (pre-isSpritePara) server, so 46/62 sprites are rc.idx-corrupt (merged/collapsed) and streak under the de-guarded identity path (expected — corrupt input). A FRESH capture from the rebuilt headless binary (isSpritePara active) yields all-clean [P,C,A,B] sprites for which the identity order spells the FULL names (leading letters included). The dev headless binary was rebuilt with the isSpritePara capture (md5 see source:hud_engineorder_staged_binary); NOT yet deployed (user-coordinated). The client de-heuristic is committed+pushed; the server is staged.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-14';

UPSERT source:hud_engineorder_staged_binary SET kind='oracle',
  ref='dev box ssh tris@65.109.77.178: cmake --build ~/projects/maplecast-flycast/build-headless -j32 (MAPLECAST_HEADLESS=ON), with core/network/maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp synced to local HEAD 6b28bac21 (the isSpritePara raw-order capture; .h + maplecast_replica_live.cpp already md5-identical dd306546/06bf091e). Staged at /tmp/flycast-engineorder-staged.',
  note='THE STAGED HEADLESS BINARY for the engine-order HUD fix. md5 = 1a07ccba034a83804e5ac9901e6e86a8 (26211840 bytes, stripped; raw==stripped). Built clean (only -Wmisleading-indentation warnings, [2/2] Linking CXX executable flycast). Symbol check: `strings flycast | grep -c MAPLECAST_HUD_TA` = 5 (HUDQ feature present). Source landmark confirmed in the built tree: collectHudQuads L3025 isSpritePara=((pcw>>29)&7)==5, L3037 seen==0 reads rc.verts[pp.first..+4] DIRECTLY for sprites (the raw [P,C,A,B] expansion order). NOT DEPLOYED — prod swap + restart is user-coordinated (per deploy-headless.sh discipline: backup the running /usr/local/bin/flycast, md5-verify before/after, ensure MAPLECAST_HUD_TA=1 stays in /etc/maplecast/headless.env, restart maplecast-headless.service). After deploy, a FRESH HUDQ capture should show all 62 name sprites as clean [P,C,A,B] parallelograms (vs 16/62 clean on the old-server _hud_cap_namegap), and the client identity-order buildHudTA spells the FULL names incl leading letters.';

RELATE finding:hud_sprite_engine_order_replaces_heuristic->cites->source:hud_sprite_expand_engine_order;
RELATE finding:hud_sprite_engine_order_replaces_heuristic->cites->source:hud_engineorder_staged_binary;
RELATE finding:hud_sprite_engine_order_replaces_heuristic->supersedes->finding:hud_sprite_client_fix_shipped;
RELATE finding:hud_sprite_engine_order_replaces_heuristic->about->finding:hud_sprite_capture_server_bug;
RELATE finding:hud_sprite_engine_order_replaces_heuristic->about->finding:hud_sprite_paratype5_client_recipe;

-- ============================================================================
-- 36i (2026-06-15): FRESH POST-DEPLOY CAPTURE from the LIVE engine-order binary
-- (md5 1a07ccba, NOW on prod 149.28.44.118). FIRST verification that the
-- isSpritePara server fix took on a running-binary capture (all prior tests reused
-- the OLD buggy capture). TWO results: (1) the SERVER FIX TOOK — sprites are clean
-- raw [P,C,A,B]; (2) the names/sprites STILL garble — the order theory is now
-- EXHAUSTED; the residual is the fmt=5 PAL4 SPRITE-TEXTURE DECODE, not corner order.
-- feat/render-replica-live. (render-pipeline expert; mvc2-sprite-render owner.)
-- ============================================================================

UPSERT source:hud_fresh_postdeploy_capture_2026_06_15 SET kind='oracle',
  ref='node tools/render-replica-poc/hudq_capture.mjs --url wss://nobd.net/replica-live (FIRST capture from the LIVE engine-order binary md5 1a07ccba): _hud_cap_fresh2 (vframe 875729, 57 quads, 5 ParaType-5 sprites) + _hud_cap_fresh3 (vframe 882168, 61 quads, 8 ParaType-5 sprites). Plane-test verdict: tools/render-replica-poc/_sprite_order_verdict.mjs (per-sprite: identify P via UV plane-interpolation residual + identity-strip non-bowtie test, using the CORRECT pvr2 _buildIndexBuffer triangulation tris (0,1,2)+(2,1,3)). Verbatim render: tools/render-replica-poc/_render_fresh.mjs / _render_sprites_only.mjs / _decode_sprite_tex.mjs (real pvr2-renderer + texture-manager + ta-parser, Dawn).',
  note='FRESH POST-DEPLOY CAPTURE FROM THE RUNNING BINARY (user in a live match). SERVER-FIX-TOOK VERDICT (the question every prior test dodged by reusing the old capture): of the ParaType-5 sprites in BOTH fresh captures, P is at index 0 (raw [P,C,A,B] expansion order) in 5/5 AND 8/8 = 13/13 = 100%, all PLANAR (UV plane-interp residual = 0.0e0), all identity-strip VALID (non-bowtie). CONTRAST the OLD buggy-server _hud_cap_namegap (same verdict tool): P-at-0 only 10/62, 40/62 bowtie. => the isSpritePara rc.verts-direct read (maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp collectHudQuads L3025-3047; landmine cleared: ta_util.cpp sortTriangles reads pp.first as a verts offset and NEVER rewrites it, so the contiguous rc.verts[pp.first..+4] read is correct in autosort AND non-autosort) IS WORKING on the deployed binary. The server fix is CONFIRMED LIVE-CORRECT. BUT rendering _hud_cap_fresh3 through the VERBATIM client path (current replay.html buildHudTA identity [0,1,2,3] + pvr2): the para4 polys (HP bars, portraits, FONT-frame name text "TRM"/"INEL"/"3LE") render CLEAN, while ALL 8 ParaType-5 sprites (bottom-center: 2 big PAL4 portrait/super sprites x174-281 + 6 meter-level-digit sprites x530-672) render as PAL4 COLOUR-NOISE SPECKLE despite the clean [P,C,A,B] geometry. Standalone-decoding the sprite TEXTURE (tcw 2a082c00 addr 0x416000 / 2b083100 addr 0x418800, TextureManager.getTexture) yields NOISE at the TSP-derived 32x32 but recognizable image FRAGMENTS at 128x128 — the VRAM is POPULATED (~50% non-zero, structured PAL4 nibble runs) and the palette banks (16/24 = P1C1/P2C1 char banks) are shipped, so the garble is a TEXTURE-DECODE problem (dims/twiddle/palette-format for these fmt=5 PAL4 sprite textures), NOT corner order and NOT a VRAM/palette coverage gap.';

UPSERT finding:hud_name_garble_is_texture_decode_not_order SET
  statement='THE NAME/SPRITE GARBLE IS THE fmt=5 PAL4 SPRITE-TEXTURE DECODE, NOT the corner/strip order. The order theory is now EXHAUSTED by FRESH POST-DEPLOY DATA (source:hud_fresh_postdeploy_capture_2026_06_15): on the LIVE engine-order binary (md5 1a07ccba) every captured ParaType-5 sprite is clean raw [P,C,A,B] (P at index 0, planar UV residual 0.0, identity-strip non-bowtie) in 13/13 sprites — the server isSpritePara fix DID take (vs 10/62 on the old buggy server). YET the sprites STILL render as PAL4 colour-noise through the verbatim client pvr2 path, while the ParaType-4 polys (bars/portraits/FONT-frame name text) in the SAME frame render perfectly. So coercing the sprite to a polygon + identity strip is geometrically correct but does NOT fix the garble — the residual is the TEXTURE. EVIDENCE: standalone TextureManager.getTexture(tsp 949004d2 -> 32x32, tcw 2a082c00 fmt=5 PAL4 scan=0-twiddled palSel16, addr 0x416000) = speckle noise; the VRAM at the sprite addrs is POPULATED (structured nibble runs ~50% non-zero) and palSel 16/24 palette banks are shipped — so it is a DECODE bug (wrong dims, wrong twiddle lattice, or wrong palette interpretation for these sprite textures), localizable but OUTSIDE the strip-order client fix. TCW union note (flycast core/hw/pvr/ta_structs.h): for fmt 5/6 (paletted) bits21-26 are the 6-bit PalSelect and OVERLAP StrideSel(25)/ScanOrder(26); the client reads palSel=(tcw>>21)&0x3F (correct) and scan=(tcw>>26)&1 (top palSel bit; =0 here -> treats as twiddled). WHETHER these sprite textures are truly 32x32-twiddled-PAL4 or a stride/linear/different-dim layout is the open decode question — DEFER to mvc2-sh4-re-expert (owns PVR raster/texture semantics): determine the correct sample for a HUD ParaType-5 PAL4 sprite (dims source, twiddle vs linear, palette format) so texture-manager.mjs decodes it to the real glyph/portrait. SUPERSEDES the implicit premise of finding:hud_sprite_engine_order_replaces_heuristic that fixing capture-order would spell the full names — order is now PROVEN fixed AND the names still garble; the next fix is the texture decode, not the wire/order.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-15';

UPSERT finding:hud_server_isspritepara_fix_took SET
  statement='THE SERVER isSpritePara CAPTURE FIX IS CONFIRMED LIVE-CORRECT (the question 3 prior "validations" never answered because they reused the OLD-binary capture). FRESH captures from the deployed engine-order binary (md5 1a07ccba, prod 149.28.44.118) show 13/13 ParaType-5 sprites in raw [P,C,A,B] order (P at index 0, planar, identity-strip valid), vs 10/62 on the pre-fix _hud_cap_namegap. GROUNDING the correctness: collectHudQuads (maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp) for isSpritePara=((pcw>>29)&7)==5 SKIPS the rc.idx walk (if(!isSpritePara)) so seen stays 0 and the seen==0 branch reads rc.verts[pp.first..pp.first+count] DIRECTLY; ta_util.cpp sortTriangles reads pp.first as a ctx.verts offset (&ctx.verts[pp.first]) and NEVER writes pp.first (it only appends to ctx.idx + builds sortedTriangles), so the contiguous verts read is correct in BOTH the autosort-tr and non-autosort cases — no remaining server bug. NO further server change is needed for the name SPRITES\' geometry; the residual garble is the client-side texture decode (finding:hud_name_garble_is_texture_decode_not_order). NOTE: this fresh-capture session caught only the meter-level-digit + super/portrait PAL4 sprites (the per-character BIG-NAME PAL4 plates were not emitted this frame — the names rendered via para4 FONT-frame polys), but the verdict holds for every ParaType-5 sprite present and the decode bug is identical across all fmt=5 PAL4 HUD sprites.',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-15';

UPSERT finding:hud_render_mode_debug_toggle SET
  statement='USER-BROWSER VALIDATION TOGGLE shipped in replay.html (renderHudQuads): window._hudRenderMode switches the engine-HUDQ draw between \'engine\' (default: all quads), \'no-sprites\' (draw only ParaType-4 polygons, SKIP the garbling ParaType-5 sprites), and \'sprites-only\' (only sprites). Proven through the verbatim pvr2 path on _hud_cap_fresh3: \'no-sprites\' renders a FULLY CLEAN HUD (HP bars + portraits + FONT-frame name text), isolating the garble to the ParaType-5 sprites; \'engine\' shows the full set with the bottom-center sprite noise. This is the REAL-BROWSER A/B check (the offline Dawn harness mis-validated 3x by sharing buildHudTA logic). Cache-bust bumped ?v=scene1 -> ?v=scene2 across replay.html module imports; title tag -> hud:ui2-spritedbg. The toggle is a debug aid, NOT the fix — the fix is the fmt=5 PAL4 sprite-texture decode (deferred to mvc2-sh4-re-expert).',
  status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-06-15';

RELATE finding:hud_name_garble_is_texture_decode_not_order->cites->source:hud_fresh_postdeploy_capture_2026_06_15;
